  ["Bahasa Inggris||Culture||Indonesian Folktales"]: [
    {"question":"What is the moral lesson of the folktale 'Bawang Merah Bawang Putih'?","options":["Always be kind and honest","Never listen to your parents","It is good to be lazy","Stealing is acceptable"],"correctIndex":0,"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The story teaches that being kind and good will be rewarded, while being evil and selfish will be punished. Bawang Putih is kind and succeeds, while Bawang Merah is cruel and fails."},
    {"question":"What is the moral of the story 'The Tortoise and the Hare'?","options":["Slow and steady wins the race.","Fast is always best.","Never take a nap.","Tortoises are better than hares."],"correctIndex":0,"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The tortoise wins by moving slowly but never stopping, so the story teaches that slow and steady wins the race."},
    {"question":"In the fable 'The Lion and the Mouse', who helps the lion get free from the net?","options":["A cat","A mouse","A bird","A snake"],"correctIndex":1,"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The small mouse chews the ropes of the net and frees the lion, showing that even a tiny animal can help."},
    {"question":"What does 'Timun Mas' mean in English?","options":["Golden Cucumber","Red Onion","White Garlic","Golden Snail"],"correctIndex":0,"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"Timun means cucumber and Mas means gold or golden, so Timun Mas means Golden Cucumber. It is the name of a girl in an Indonesian folktale."},
    {"question":"In 'The Fox and the Grapes', the fox cannot reach the grapes and says they are sour. What does this teach us?","options":["Foxes like red grapes.","We should not say something is bad just because we cannot have it.","Grapes grow on low branches.","Mice love to eat grapes."],"correctIndex":1,"difficulty":"hard","explanation":"The fox wanted the grapes but could not reach them, so he said they were sour. The story teaches us not to pretend things are bad just because we cannot get them."},
    {"question":"In the folktale 'Sangkuriang', what did Dayang Sumbi do when Sangkuriang wanted to marry her?","options":["She agreed to marry him","She refused and gave him impossible tasks","She turned him into a dog","She left the village forever"],"correctIndex":1,"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"Dayang Sumbi recognized Sangkuriang as her own son because of a scar. She did not want to marry him, so she asked him to build a lake and a boat in one night, which was impossible."},
    {"question":"Which fable shows that being kind to others can bring help when you need it?","options":["The Ant and the Grasshopper","The Lion and the Mouse","The Boy Who Cried Wolf","The Fox and the Grapes"],"correctIndex":1,"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"In The Lion and the Mouse, the lion is kind to the mouse and later the mouse helps the lion. This shows kindness can be rewarded."},
    {"question":"A boy cried 'wolf' for fun. When a real wolf came, no one helped him. What is the moral?","options":["Wolves are dangerous animals.","Always tell the truth.","Sheep should stay inside.","Climbing hills is fun."],"correctIndex":1,"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"Because the boy lied, people did not believe him when he told the truth. The story teaches us to always tell the truth."},
    {"question":"Which Indonesian folktale comes from Bali and tells about a widow who uses black magic?","options":["Calon Arang","Malin Kundang","Sangkuriang","Timun Mas"],"correctIndex":0,"difficulty":"hard","explanation":"Calon Arang is a Balinese folktale about a widow who practiced black magic and caused trouble in her village. The other stories are from different regions and have different plots."},
    {"question":"Which Indonesian folktale is about a boy who turned into a stone because he disobeyed his mother?","options":["Malin Kundang","Sangkuriang","Timun Mas","Bawang Merah Bawang Putih"],"correctIndex":0,"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"Malin Kundang is a famous Indonesian folktale from West Sumatra about a boy who became a stone after he was cursed by his mother for being ungrateful."},
    {"question":"In the story of Malin Kundang, what happened to Malin Kundang after he denied his mother?","options":["He became a wealthy merchant","He helped his mother","He turned into a stone","He married a princess"],"correctIndex":2,"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"Malin Kundang was cursed by his mother and turned into a stone because he was ashamed of her."},
    {"question":"In the legend of Roro Jonggrang, what did Bandung Bondowoso ask Roro Jonggrang to do?","options":["Build 1,000 temples in one night","Find a golden egg","Make a thousand wells","Weave a cloth"],"correctIndex":0,"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"Bandung Bondowoso asked Roro Jonggrang to build 1,000 temples in one night as a condition to marry her."},
    {"question":"Who is the main character in the story of Tangkuban Perahu?","options":["Dayang Sumbi","Roro Jonggrang","Malin Kundang","Cinderella"],"correctIndex":0,"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"Tangkuban Perahu is about Dayang Sumbi and her son Sangkuriang, which led to the creation of Mount Tangkuban Perahu."},
    {"question":"What is the moral lesson of the folktale Bawang Merah Bawang Putih?","options":["Be honest","Be kind to others","Do not be greedy","All of the above"],"correctIndex":3,"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The story teaches multiple values such as honesty, kindness, and the consequences of greed."},
    {"question":"In the story of Keong Emas (Golden Snail), who was turned into a golden snail?","options":["A princess","A witch","A farmer","A prince"],"correctIndex":0,"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"A princess was cursed by an evil witch and transformed into a golden snail."},
  ],

